<h1>Two balls of the same colour</h1>
<div class="tagline"><span class="chip">#counting</span><span class="chip">#draws</span></div>
<section class="sheet"><h2 class="label">Statement</h2><div class="body"><p>A bag contains <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span></span></span></span> red balls and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span></span></span></span> blue balls. Two balls are drawn at random without replacement. What is the probability that they have the same colour?</p></div></section>
<details class="hint"><summary>Hint</summary><div class="body"><p>Count the pairs of balls: all pairs, then the pairs of the same colour.</p></div></details>
